# On Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm (labwc/Wayland, the default on Pi 4/5),
# labwc reads ~/.config/labwc/autostart as a shell script, not a
# freedesktop .desktop file despite the filename here. Append this line to
# that file (create it if it doesn't exist):
#
#   systemctl --user start p1s-touchscreen.service &
#
# This is a thin trigger -- p1s-touchscreen.service (see
# p1s-touchscreen.service in this directory) does the actual work and gives
# you Restart=on-failure for free, which a bare autostart script launching
# main.py directly would not.
#
# One-time setup:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
#   cp deploy/p1s-touchscreen.service ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user enable p1s-touchscreen.service
#
# Screen blanking: labwc's idle/DPMS config surface has moved around across
# Bookworm point releases. Check `labwc --help` / ~/.config/labwc/rc.xml on
# your image for the current <idle> or DPMS settings, or disable blanking at
# the kernel/compositor level (e.g. `wlopm --off` equivalents) -- verify on
# the actual target OS image rather than assuming one fixed incantation.
